  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lokesh vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 17 May, 2022 Author: Subodh Abhyankar Bench: Subodh Abhyankar 1 Mcrc No.23947/2022 High Court of Madhya Pradesh, Jabalpur Bench at Indore Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Subodh Abhyankar On The 17Th Of May, 2022 Miscellaneous Criminal Case No.23947/2022 Between: - Lokesh S/o Mangilal Patidar, Caste: Kulmi, Age- 41 years, Occupation- Business, Jitendra S/o Ramesh Chandra Soni, Caste: Soni, Age- 40 years, Occupation- Business, Both R/o: Manawar, District Dhar (Mp) .....Applicants (By Shri Ashish Gupta, Advocate) And The State of Madhya Pradesh Through Police Station Manawar, Dhar District Dhar (Mp) .....Respondent (By Shri Akash Sharma, Government Advocate)",
    "facts": "This is applicants' first application under Section 438 of Criminal Procedure Code, 1973 for grant of anticipatory bail, as the present applicant (s) is apprehending his / her arrest in connection with Crime No.188/2022 registered at Police Station Manawar, District Dhar (MP) for offence punishable under Sections 420, 272 and 273 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and also under Section 3 read with Section 7 of the Essential Commodities Act, 1955. The allegation against the applicants is that of selling substandard Pan Masala, which was being sold in the name of \"Pan Bahar Khandani Pan Masala\". Counsel for the applicants has submitted that the aforesaid product was purchased by the applicants from some other person; and in fact, its manufacture is at New Delhi only and address of which has also been furnished to the respondent / Food Department and a notice under Rule 2.4.2 (6) of Food Safety and Standard Rules 2011 has also been issued to the said manufacturer including the present applicants. Counsel has also submitted that even according to the Police Prativedan, the statements of the applicants have also been recorded by the prosecution / Food Department and at this juncture, their custodial interrogation is not necessary, as the charge sheet is about to be filed, as no further recovery or discovery is to be made at their instance. It is further submitted that the applicants were given a notice under Section 41-A of the Cr.P.C.",
    "arguments": "It is submitted that in case of their arrest, an irreparable injury shall be caused to their reputation. Counsel has submitted that even otherwise, the applicant (s) is ready to cooperate with the investigation and no purpose would be served in sending the applicant (s) behind the bars.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted that in case of their arrest, an irreparable injury shall be caused to their reputation. Counsel has submitted that even otherwise, the applicant (s) is ready to cooperate with the investigation and no purpose would be served in sending the applicant (s) behind the bars.",
